     Executed 69 tests, with 0 failures (0 unexpected).
     Building the package proves all four core sources compile under Swift 6 strict concurrency.
     NOTE: an initial run caught a real bug — Swift treats CRLF ("\r\n") as ONE Character grapheme, so the
     first Character-based separator set missed it; splitTokens was rewritten to iterate Unicode scalars
     (matching JavaScript's UTF-16 split). Re-run: green. This is why the real XCTest suites were executed,
     not merely asserted.

